  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh - Flash Floods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aid is focused on the most affected districts in the northern, northeastern, and southeastern regions of Bangladesh, such as Sylhet, Jamalpur, Kurigram, Gaibandha, Bogura, Sirajganj, Tangail, Noakhali, and Feni.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The beneficiaries include 400,000 people, prioritized by vulnerability, particularly displaced individuals, households with damaged homes, female-headed households, elderly people, children, pregnant women, and people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation includes distributing multipurpose cash grants, food, shelter materials, hygiene kits, deploying mobile medical teams, and restoring damaged water sources and sanitation facilities to support immediate needs and long-term recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This response is needed due to severe flooding across Bangladesh, which has displaced millions, destroyed homes, and compromised essential infrastructure, leaving people without access to clean water, food, and healthcare.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide urgent humanitarian assistance following severe floods in Bangladesh that have impacted millions of people by destroying infrastructure, displacing communities, and disrupting access to basic necessities such as clean water, food, shelter, and healthcare.</narrative>
  </description>
